note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note omegallm serve.om (aien-train DRA-119): `ollm serve PORT CK MERGES [MAXCONN]`, an
note OpenAI-compatible HTTP/1.1 server for a v1 BPE checkpoint (V > 256) on 127.0.0.1:PORT only.
note aarch64 only: build.sh composes it under one `om2` line after the omega-mv e5b32567 units
note net/http.om, net/json.om and net/jsonw.om (vendored unmodified); the other targets take
note noserve.om. It prints `PORT n`, then serves one connection at a time, one request each
note (Connection: close), until MAXCONN connections (default 1000000) have been served.
note Routes: GET /health {"status":"ok","in_flight":0}; GET /v1/models; POST /v1/chat/completions
note with JSON or SSE (stream true) responses; other paths 404, other methods 405.
note Request: messages (non-empty array of objects with a string role of at most 32 bytes and a
note string or null content), optional max_tokens or max_completion_tokens (1 .. 999999),
note temperature (0 .. 2 without exponent, used to 0.001; default 1), seed (unsigned, default 1),
note stream, stream_options.include_usage and n (only 1). Other members (model, tools, tool_choice)
note are accepted and ignored: this model never calls tools.
note Interim chat template (until DRA-123 fixes one shared template): `role: content\n` for each
note message in order, then `assistant: `; at most 4000 bytes, else 400. The context is token 0 then
note the template's encoding (CT0 tokens, reported as prompt_tokens); CT0 >= T is refused with 400
note context_length_exceeded. Output runs at most min(max_tokens, T - CT0) tokens, so the T-token
note window never slides (cmdsamp's sampling step osstep, splitmix64 seed stream); a generated
note token 0 ends it with finish_reason stop, the limit with length. Decoded bytes are sent as
note UTF-8: a sequence cut by a token boundary waits for the next token, an ill-formed one (or one
note cut by the end) becomes U+FFFD. One line per routed response (and per 413 at the head) goes
note to stdout: `C status prompt_tokens completion_tokens finish(0 none, 1 stop, 2 length) ms`.
note Exit codes: 2 usage; 27 merges (bpe.om); 71 the port cannot be bound.
note wb layout: raw token bytes [0, 8192), content [8192, 73728), template [73728, 77824),
note message [81920, 82176), response id [82176, 82240). sv slots: 0 stream, 1 max tokens,
note 2 TEMPMILLI, 3 seed state, 4 include_usage, 5 template bytes, 6 CT0, 7 generated, 8 finish,
note 9 request count, 10 created, 11 start ns, 12 raw bytes, 13 content bytes, 14 content sent,
note 16 error code, 19 T, 21 last status.

text svtjson "application/json"
text svtctyp "Content-Type"
text svphlth "/health"
text svpmods "/v1/models"
text svpchat "/v1/chat/completions"
text svmget "GET"
text svmpost "POST"
text svthlth "{\"status\":\"ok\",\"in_flight\":0}"
text svtmods "{\"object\":\"list\",\"data\":[{\"id\":\"ollm\",\"object\":\"model\",\"created\":0,\"owned_by\":\"aien\"}]}"
text svport "PORT "
text skmsgs "messages"
text skrole "role"
text skcont "content"
text skstrm "stream"
text skmaxt "max_tokens"
text skmaxc "max_completion_tokens"
text sktemp "temperature"
text skseed "seed"
text skopts "stream_options"
text skincl "include_usage"
text skn "n"
text skid "id"
text skobj "object"
text skcrt "created"
text skmodel "model"
text skchoi "choices"
text skidx "index"
text skmsg "message"
text skdelta "delta"
text skfin "finish_reason"
text skusage "usage"
text skpt "prompt_tokens"
text skct "completion_tokens"
text sktt "total_tokens"
text skerr "error"
text sktype "type"
text skcode "code"
text skparam "param"
text svollm "ollm"
text svasst "assistant"
text svcc "chat.completion"
text svccc "chat.completion.chunk"
text svstop "stop"
text svlen "length"
text svinv "invalid_request_error"
text svsrv "server_error"
text svdone "[DONE]"
text svidp "chatcmpl-ollm-"
text svsep ": "
text svnl "\n"
text svaprm "assistant: "
text secjson "invalid_json"
text secreq "invalid_request"
text secctx "context_length_exceeded"
text secbig "request_too_large"
text secnf "not_found"
text secmeth "method_not_allowed"
text secint "internal_error"
text sem1 "request body is not valid JSON (RFC 8259) or has over 65532 JSON tokens"
text sem2 "the request must be a JSON object"
text sem3 "messages must be a non-empty array of objects"
text sem4 "message content must be a string or null"
text sem5 "message role must be a string of at most 32 bytes"
text sem6 "the chat template is over 4000 bytes"
text sem7 "temperature must be a number from 0 to 2 without exponent"
text sem8 "max_tokens must be an integer from 1 to 999999"
text sem9 "seed must be an unsigned integer"
text sem10 "stream must be true or false"
text sem12 "only n = 1 is supported"
text sem13 "the request body is over 983040 bytes"
text sem14 "no such path; routes: GET /health, GET /v1/models, POST /v1/chat/completions"
text sem15 "method not allowed on this path"
text sem16 "response construction failed"
text sem11a "prompt is "
text sem11b " tokens including the start token; the context window is "
text sem11c " tokens, so no room is left for output"

note ======== small byte helpers over wb

note svmcat: copy text t into wb at p, at most up to e; the next p
fn svmcat wb edit uchar 82432 p ulong e ulong t view uchar * to ulong
q = p
for i ulong len t
if ge q e
ret q
end
put wb q get t i
q = add q 1
end
ret q
end

note svmdec: v in decimal into wb at p (at most 20 digits, up to e); the next p
fn svmdec wb edit uchar 82432 p ulong e ulong v ulong to ulong
d = new uchar 20 0
i = ulong 20
x = v
for it ulong 20
i = sub i 1
put d i uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
break
end
end
q = p
for k ulong sub 20 i
if ge q e
ret q
end
put wb q get d add i k
q = add q 1
end
ret q
end

note ======== UTF-8 (RFC 3629 section 4)

note svu8n: the sequence at a[p], with a[0 .. n) the bytes so far: 1 .. 4 its length when well
note formed; 0 when a[p .. n) is a proper prefix of a well-formed sequence; 8 + k when its maximal
note ill-formed subpart is k bytes (replaced by one U+FFFD)
fn svu8n a view uchar * p ulong n ulong to ulong
c = ulong get a p
if lt c 128
ret 1
end
k = svu8k c
if eq k 0
ret 9
end
for i ulong sub k 1
q = add p add i 1
if ge q n
ret 0
end
if not svu8ok c i ulong get a q
ret add 9 i
end
end
ret k
end

note svu8k: the sequence length a lead byte c >= 128 starts, 0 when it starts none
fn svu8k c ulong to ulong
if and ge c 194 le c 223
ret 2
end
if and ge c 224 le c 239
ret 3
end
if and ge c 240 le c 244
ret 4
end
ret 0
end

note svu8ok: whether b may be continuation byte i (0 the first) after lead byte c (RFC 3629 table)
fn svu8ok c ulong i ulong b ulong to bool
lo = ulong 128
hi = ulong 191
if eq i 0
if eq c 224
lo = 160
end
if eq c 237
hi = 159
end
if eq c 240
lo = 144
end
if eq c 244
hi = 143
end
end
ret and ge b lo le b hi
end

note svrepl: U+FFFD (EF BF BD) into the content at its end
fn svrepl wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to void
g = add 8192 get sv 13
put wb g 239
put wb add g 1 191
put wb add g 2 189
put sv 13 add get sv 13 3
end

note svclean: move the complete sequences of the raw bytes wb[0, sv12) to the content; fin 1 also
note replaces a cut tail. The rest moves to the front of the raw bytes.
fn svclean wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 fin ulong to void
rn = get sv 12
p = ulong 0
for it ulong add rn 1
if ge p rn
break
end
r = svu8n wb p rn
if eq r 0
if eq fin 0
break
end
svrepl wb sv
p = rn
else
if gt r 8
svrepl wb sv
p = add p sub r 8
else
svmove wb add 8192 get sv 13 p r
put sv 13 add get sv 13 r
p = add p r
end
end
end
svmove wb 0 p sub rn p
put sv 12 sub rn p
end

note svmove: wb[d, d + n) = wb[s, s + n), copying forward (d <= s or the ranges apart)
fn svmove wb edit uchar 82432 d ulong s ulong n ulong to void
for i ulong n
put wb add d i get wb add s i
end
end

note ======== responses

fn svstat cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 code ulong t view uchar * to long
r = hrspst cs io code
r = hfe r hhname cs io svtctyp
r = hfe r hhval cs io svtjson
r = hfe r hhend cs io 0 len t
r = hfe r hput cs io t
ret hfe r hwfin cs io
end

note svsend: the writer's text ob[1040, 1040 + n) as a JSON response with status code
fn svsend cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 ob edit uchar 409600 code ulong n ulong to long
r = hrspst cs io code
r = hfe r hhname cs io svtctyp
r = hfe r hhval cs io svtjson
r = hfe r hhend cs io 0 n
r = hfe r hput cs io view part ob 1040 n
ret hfe r hwfin cs io
end

fn svwt ob edit uchar 409600 t view uchar * to void
js_wsbuf ob t 0 len t
end

note svemsg: the message of error code sv16 into wb[81920 ..); its length
fn svemsg wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to ulong
e = get sv 16
b = ulong 81920
z = ulong 82176
p = b
if eq e 1
p = svmcat wb p z sem1
end
if eq e 2
p = svmcat wb p z sem2
end
if eq e 3
p = svmcat wb p z sem3
end
if eq e 4
p = svmcat wb p z sem4
end
if eq e 5
p = svmcat wb p z sem5
end
if eq e 6
p = svmcat wb p z sem6
end
if eq e 7
p = svmcat wb p z sem7
end
if eq e 8
p = svmcat wb p z sem8
end
if eq e 9
p = svmcat wb p z sem9
end
if eq e 10
p = svmcat wb p z sem10
end
if eq e 11
p = svmcat wb p z sem11a
p = svmdec wb p z get sv 6
p = svmcat wb p z sem11b
p = svmdec wb p z get sv 19
p = svmcat wb p z sem11c
end
if eq e 12
p = svmcat wb p z sem12
end
if eq e 13
p = svmcat wb p z sem13
end
if eq e 14
p = svmcat wb p z sem14
end
if eq e 15
p = svmcat wb p z sem15
end
if eq e 16
p = svmcat wb p z sem16
end
ret sub p b
end

fn svecode ob edit uchar 409600 e ulong to void
if eq e 1
svwt ob secjson
ret
end
if eq e 11
svwt ob secctx
ret
end
if eq e 13
svwt ob secbig
ret
end
if eq e 14
svwt ob secnf
ret
end
if eq e 15
svwt ob secmeth
ret
end
if eq e 16
svwt ob secint
ret
end
svwt ob secreq
end

note svfail: {"error":{"message","type","param":null,"code"}} for error code sv16 with status st
fn svfail cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 st ulong to long
ob = new uchar 409600 0
put sv 21 st
m = svemsg wb sv
x = js_winit ob
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skerr
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skmsg
js_wsbuf ob wb 81920 m
svwt ob sktype
if eq st 500
svwt ob svsrv
else
svwt ob svinv
end
svwt ob skparam
js_wnull ob
svwt ob skcode
svecode ob get sv 16
js_wobje ob
js_wobje ob
n = js_wdone ob
if lt n 0
put cs HKEEP 0
ret hrsperr cs io 500
end
ret svsend cs io ob st ulong n
end

note svhead: {"id", "object" t, "created", "model" opened; the caller adds the rest
fn svhead ob edit uchar 409600 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 t view uchar * to void
x = js_winit ob
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skid
js_wsbuf ob wb 82176 get sv 15
svwt ob skobj
svwt ob t
svwt ob skcrt
js_wulong ob get sv 10
svwt ob skmodel
svwt ob svollm
end

fn svfr ob edit uchar 409600 sv edit ulong 64 to void
f = get sv 8
if eq f 1
svwt ob svstop
ret
end
if eq f 2
svwt ob svlen
ret
end
js_wnull ob
end

fn svusage ob edit uchar 409600 sv edit ulong 64 to void
svwt ob skusage
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skpt
js_wulong ob get sv 6
svwt ob skct
js_wulong ob get sv 7
svwt ob sktt
js_wulong ob add get sv 6 get sv 7
js_wobje ob
end

note svfull: the chat.completion object (stream false)
fn svfull ob edit uchar 409600 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to long
svhead ob wb sv svcc
svwt ob skchoi
js_warr ob
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skidx
js_wulong ob 0
svwt ob skmsg
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skrole
svwt ob svasst
svwt ob skcont
js_wsbuf ob wb 8192 get sv 13
js_wobje ob
svwt ob skfin
svfr ob sv
js_wobje ob
js_warre ob
svusage ob sv
js_wobje ob
ret js_wdone ob
end

note svchunk: one chat.completion.chunk; kind 0 the role, 1 the content wb[8192 + sv14, 8192 + sv13),
note 2 the finish reason, 3 usage (empty choices). Sends it as one SSE event.
fn svchunk cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 ob edit uchar 409600 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 kind ulong to long
svhead ob wb sv svccc
svwt ob skchoi
js_warr ob
if ne kind 3
js_wobj ob
svwt ob skidx
js_wulong ob 0
svwt ob skdelta
js_wobj ob
if eq kind 0
svwt ob skrole
svwt ob svasst
svwt ob skcont
note "" as zero bytes of a non-empty text: under omc e5b32567 an empty text passed as a view has a
note wrong length (omega-mv#775, fixed after this pin), and js_wsbuf then refuses it (jswearg)
js_wsbuf ob svasst 0 0
end
if eq kind 1
svwt ob skcont
g0 = get sv 14
js_wsbuf ob wb add 8192 g0 sub get sv 13 g0
end
js_wobje ob
svwt ob skfin
if eq kind 2
svfr ob sv
else
js_wnull ob
end
js_wobje ob
end
js_warre ob
if eq kind 3
svusage ob sv
end
js_wobje ob
n = js_wdone ob
if lt n 0
ret -5
end
r = hssedat cs io view part ob 1040 ulong n
ret hfe r hsseend cs io
end

note ======== request parsing

note svtemp: the temperature token's lexeme at bd[o, o + n) as TEMPMILLI (digits, optional
note fraction, used to 0.001), or 999999 when it is not a number from 0 to 2
fn svtemp bd edit uchar 983040 o ulong n ulong to ulong
ip = ulong 0
fr = ulong 0
fd = ulong 0
dot = false
for i ulong n
c = ulong get bd add o i
if eq c 46
if dot
ret 999999
end
dot = true
else
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 999999
end
if dot
if lt fd 3
fr = add mul fr 10 sub c 48
fd = add fd 1
end
else
if ge ip 100
ret 999999
end
ip = add mul ip 10 sub c 48
end
end
end
for k ulong 3
if lt fd 3
fr = mul fr 10
fd = add fd 1
end
end
m = add mul ip 1000 fr
if gt m 2000
ret 999999
end
ret m
end

note svpcat: append text t to the template; false when it would pass 4000 bytes
fn svpcat wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 t view uchar * to bool
pl = get sv 5
if gt add pl len t 4000
ret false
end
for i ulong len t
put wb add 73728 add pl i get t i
end
put sv 5 add pl len t
ret true
end

note svpstr: append the decoded string token t (role or content) to the template
fn svpstr bd edit uchar 983040 tp edit uint 262144 t ulong wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to bool
pl = get sv 5
if ge pl 4000
ret false
end
n = js_sget bd js_off tp t part wb add 73728 pl sub 4000 pl
if lt n 0
ret false
end
put sv 5 add pl ulong n
ret true
end

note svmsg1: one message object e into the template; 0 or an error code
fn svmsg1 bd edit uchar 983040 tp edit uint 262144 e ulong wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to ulong
if ne js_type tp e 1
ret 3
end
ro = jsnone
co = jsnone
k = js_first tp e
for it ulong js_nkids tp e
if eq k jsnone
break
end
o = js_off tp k
if js_streq bd o skrole
ro = add k 1
end
if js_streq bd o skcont
co = add k 1
end
k = js_mnext tp k
end
if eq ro jsnone
ret 5
end
if or ne js_type tp ro 6 gt js_slen tp ro 32
ret 5
end
if eq co jsnone
ret 4
end
ct = js_type tp co
if and ne ct 6 ne ct 10
ret 4
end
if not svpstr bd tp ro wb sv
ret 6
end
if not svpcat wb sv svsep
ret 6
end
if eq ct 6
if not svpstr bd tp co wb sv
ret 6
end
end
if not svpcat wb sv svnl
ret 6
end
ret 0
end

fn svmsgs bd edit uchar 983040 tp edit uint 262144 a ulong wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to ulong
if ne js_type tp a 3
ret 3
end
n = js_nkids tp a
if eq n 0
ret 3
end
e = js_first tp a
for it ulong n
if eq e jsnone
break
end
r = svmsg1 bd tp e wb sv
if ne r 0
ret r
end
e = js_enext tp e
end
if not svpcat wb sv svaprm
ret 6
end
ret 0
end

note svopts: stream_options value v: include_usage true sets sv4
fn svopts bd edit uchar 983040 tp edit uint 262144 v ulong sv edit ulong 64 to void
if ne js_type tp v 1
ret
end
k = js_first tp v
for it ulong js_nkids tp v
if eq k jsnone
break
end
if js_streq bd js_off tp k skincl
if eq js_type tp add k 1 8
put sv 4 1
end
end
k = js_mnext tp k
end
end

note svscal: one scalar member (key token k, value k + 1); 0 or an error code
fn svscal bd edit uchar 983040 tp edit uint 262144 k ulong sv edit ulong 64 to ulong
o = js_off tp k
v = add k 1
ty = js_type tp v
vo = js_off tp v
if or js_streq bd o skmaxt js_streq bd o skmaxc
if eq ty 10
ret 0
end
if or ne ty 7 not js_isu bd vo
ret 8
end
x = js_tou bd vo
if or eq x 0 gt x 999999
ret 8
end
put sv 1 x
ret 0
end
if js_streq bd o sktemp
if eq ty 10
ret 0
end
if ne ty 7
ret 7
end
if ne and js_nflags tp v 5 0
ret 7
end
m = svtemp bd vo js_span tp v
if gt m 2000
ret 7
end
put sv 2 m
ret 0
end
if js_streq bd o skseed
if eq ty 10
ret 0
end
if or ne ty 7 not js_isu bd vo
ret 9
end
put sv 3 js_tou bd vo
ret 0
end
if js_streq bd o skstrm
if eq ty 8
put sv 0 1
ret 0
end
if or eq ty 9 eq ty 10
ret 0
end
ret 10
end
if js_streq bd o skn
if eq ty 10
ret 0
end
if or ne ty 7 not js_isu bd vo
ret 12
end
if ne js_tou bd vo 1
ret 12
end
ret 0
end
if js_streq bd o skopts
svopts bd tp v sv
end
ret 0
end

note svparse: the request body bd[0, n) into sv and the template; 0 or an error code
fn svparse bd edit uchar 983040 n ulong wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to ulong
tp = new uint 262144 0
x = js_init tp 983040 64
r = js_parse bd tp n
if lt r 0
ret 1
end
if ne js_type tp 0 1
ret 2
end
put sv 0 0
put sv 1 999999
put sv 2 1000
put sv 3 1
put sv 4 0
put sv 5 0
ma = jsnone
k = js_first tp 0
for it ulong js_nkids tp 0
if eq k jsnone
break
end
if js_streq bd js_off tp k skmsgs
ma = add k 1
else
e = svscal bd tp k sv
if ne e 0
ret e
end
end
k = js_mnext tp k
end
if eq ma jsnone
ret 3
end
ret svmsgs bd tp ma wb sv
end

note ======== generation

note svgen: sample up to min(sv1, T - CT0) tokens; streams chunks when sv0 is 1. 0, or negative
note when a chunk could not be sent (the client left).
fn svgen cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 ob edit uchar 409600 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to long
lim = sub get sv 19 get sv 6
if lt get sv 1 lim
lim = get sv 1
end
put sv 7 0
put sv 8 0
put sv 12 0
put sv 13 0
put sv 14 0
for g ulong lim
if not svtake wb sv
break
end
r = svpend cs io ob wb sv
if lt r 0
ret r
end
end
if eq get sv 8 0
put sv 8 2
end
svclean wb sv 1
ret svpend cs io ob wb sv
end

note svtake: one sampled token into the context and the content; false when it ends the output
note (sv8: 1 token 0, 2 the content would pass its 65536 bytes)
fn svtake wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to bool
c = svdraw sv
if eq c 0
put sv 8 1
ret false
end
if not svfits sv c
put sv 8 2
ret false
end
svcap wb sv c
svclean wb sv 0
ret true
end

note svdraw: the next token (cmdsamp's step osstep), advancing the seed stream when sampling
fn svdraw sv edit ulong 64 to ulong
st = get sv 3
tm = get sv 2
c = osstep st tm
if ne tm 0
put sv 3 add st 11400714819323198485
end
ret c
end

note svfits: whether token c's bytes fit the raw buffer (8192) and, as up to three content bytes
note each, the content (65536)
fn svfits sv edit ulong 64 c ulong to bool
tl = obtlen c
rn = add get sv 12 tl
gn = add get sv 13 mul rn 3
ret not or or gt rn 8192 gt tl 4096 gt gn 65536
end

note svcap: token c's bytes onto the raw buffer, c onto the context
fn svcap wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 c ulong to void
obtcap c
rn = get sv 12
for i ulong get obon 0
put wb add rn i get obo i
end
put sv 12 add rn get obon 0
ocpush c
put sv 7 add get sv 7 1
end

note svpend: when streaming, the content not yet sent as one chunk; 0 or the send error
fn svpend cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 ob edit uchar 409600 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to long
if or ne get sv 0 1 le get sv 13 get sv 14
ret 0
end
r = svchunk cs io ob wb sv 1
put sv 14 get sv 13
ret r
end

note svid: response id chatcmpl-ollm-<request count> into wb[82176 ..), its length into sv15
fn svid wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to void
put sv 9 add get sv 9 1
p = svmcat wb 82176 82240 svidp
p = svmdec wb p 82240 get sv 9
put sv 15 sub p 82176
end

fn svlog sv edit ulong 64 to void
oputc 67
oputc 32
oputu get sv 21
oputc 32
oputu get sv 6
oputc 32
oputu get sv 7
oputc 32
oputu get sv 8
oputc 32
oputu div sub ulong monons get sv 11 1000000
oputc 10
oflush
end

note svchat: POST /v1/chat/completions
fn svchat cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 bd edit uchar 983040 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to long
note the request's clock and log fields come from svroute (svbeg)
n = hbodyall cs io bd
if lt n 0
put cs HKEEP 0
if eq n HEBIG
put sv 16 13
r = svfail cs io wb sv 413
svlog sv
ret r
end
put sv 21 400
svlog sv
ret hrsperr cs io 400
end
note generation outlasts the 60 s body deadline: only the idle limit applies from here
hsetdl cs 0
e = svparse bd ulong n wb sv
if ne e 0
put sv 16 e
r = svfail cs io wb sv 400
svlog sv
ret r
end
pl = get sv 5
for i ulong pl
put oarg i get wb add 73728 i
end
np = obpenc pl
put og 9 0
ocpush 0
for i ulong np
if lt get og 9 get og 1
ocpush get obtk i
end
end
put sv 6 add np 1
if ge get sv 6 get sv 19
put sv 16 11
r = svfail cs io wb sv 400
svlog sv
ret r
end
svid wb sv
put sv 10 ulong div realns 1000000000
ob = new uchar 409600 0
put sv 21 200
if eq get sv 0 1
r = hrspsse cs io
r = hfe r svchunk cs io ob wb sv 0
if lt r 0
svlog sv
ret r
end
r = svgen cs io ob wb sv
if lt r 0
svlog sv
ret r
end
r = svchunk cs io ob wb sv 2
if eq get sv 4 1
r = hfe r svchunk cs io ob wb sv 3
end
r = hfe r hssedat cs io svdone
r = hfe r hsseend cs io
r = hfe r hwfin cs io
svlog sv
ret r
end
r = svgen cs io ob wb sv
m = svfull ob wb sv
if lt m 0
put sv 16 16
r = svfail cs io wb sv 500
svlog sv
ret r
end
r = svsend cs io ob 200 ulong m
svlog sv
ret r
end

fn svroute cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 bd edit uchar 983040 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to long
svbeg sv
if hispath cs io svpchat
if hismeth cs io svmpost
ret svchat cs io bd wb sv
end
ret svend cs io wb sv 15 405
end
if hispath cs io svphlth
if hismeth cs io svmget
ret svok cs io sv svthlth
end
ret svend cs io wb sv 15 405
end
if hispath cs io svpmods
if hismeth cs io svmget
ret svok cs io sv svtmods
end
ret svend cs io wb sv 15 405
end
ret svend cs io wb sv 14 404
end

note svbeg: a request's log fields cleared, its clock started
fn svbeg sv edit ulong 64 to void
put sv 11 ulong monons
put sv 6 0
put sv 7 0
put sv 8 0
end

note svend: error code e with status st, logged
fn svend cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 e ulong st ulong to long
put sv 16 e
r = svfail cs io wb sv st
svlog sv
ret r
end

note svok: the fixed JSON text t with status 200, logged
fn svok cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 sv edit ulong 64 t view uchar * to long
put sv 21 200
r = svstat cs io 200 t
svlog sv
ret r
end

note svconn: one accepted connection c carries one request, answered with Connection: close.
note Connections are served one at a time, so a kept-alive idle connection would hold the listener:
note allen-chat pools its upstream connection, and its next request queued 30 s behind the pooled
note one (the old idle limit) until this change. The head must arrive within 10 s.
fn svconn c long cs edit ulong 320 io edit uchar 131072 bd edit uchar 983040 wb edit uchar 82432 sv edit ulong 64 to void
r = hinit cs io int c 1
if lt r 0
x = hclose cs
ret
end
hsettmo cs 10000000000 10000000000
hsetbdl cs 60000000000
note the JSON parser takes at most 983040 bytes (jsmaxn); larger Content-Length is 413 at the head
put cs HBCAP 983040
r = hreqrd cs io
if eq r HEBIG
put cs HKEEP 0
svbeg sv
x = svend cs io wb sv 13 413
end
if and lt r 0 ne r HEBIG
x = hreject cs io r
end
if gt r 0
put cs HKEEP 0
x = svroute cs io bd wb sv
end
x = hclose cs
end

note serve PORT CK MERGES [MAXCONN]
fn cmdserve to void
na = oargc
if and ne na 5 ne na 6
exit 2
end
port = oargu 2
if or eq port 0 gt port 65535
exit 2
end
mx = ulong 1000000
if eq na 6
mx = oargu 5
if eq mx 0
exit 2
end
end
ockload 3
v = get og 0
obload 4 v
cs = new ulong 320 0
io = new uchar 131072 0
bd = new uchar 983040 0
wb = new uchar 82432 0
sv = new ulong 64 0
a = new uchar 16 0
put sv 19 get og 1
r = haddr4 a 2130706433 port
lf = hlisten a 16
if lt lf 0
exit 71
end
for i ulong len svport
oputc ulong get svport i
end
oputu port
oputc 10
oflush
nc = ulong 0
for j ulong 999999999
c = haccept int lf 60000000000
if ge c 0
svconn c cs io bd wb sv
nc = add nc 1
if ge nc mx
break
end
end
end
x = fclose int lf
end
